Biopython

seqblaze's tm compat="biopython" reproduces the behaviour of Biopython 1.88
Bio.SeqUtils.MeltingTemp.Tm_NN ("compatible with Biopython"; no endorsement
by the Biopython project is implied).

Consulted file:
  Bio/SeqUtils/MeltingTemp.py at git tag biopython-188
  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/biopython/biopython/biopython-188/Bio/SeqUtils/MeltingTemp.py
  sha256 4f3cbc585ffd68d54386d40f5edb113a7c2eae4aa4388c6b496bceecdec06500 (43,151 bytes)

What was used: the operation order, the unit-conversion literals and the
control flow of Tm_NN and salt_correction (method 5), for compat="biopython".
No Biopython function body and no Biopython parameter table was copied.
Tm_NN's keyword names (Na, K, Tris, Mg, dNTPs, dnac1, dnac2) and the texts of
two of its error messages are quoted for compatibility. Every parameter value
comes from the published papers through seqblaze's parameter ledger
(SantaLucia 1998, doi:10.1073/pnas.95.4.1460; von Ahsen et al. 2001,
doi:10.1093/clinchem/47.11.1956).

