Nearest Neighbor Database (NNDB), DNA parameters

seqblaze's params="santalucia2004" preset for duplex (and tm on a Pairs
input, which reads the same compiled pack) takes its 1x2, 2x1 and 2x2
internal-loop free energies and enthalpies from the "DNA (RNAstructure)"
section of the Nearest Neighbor Database (https://rna.urmc.rochester.edu/NNDB/,
snapshot collected 2026-10-16). No endorsement by the NNDB authors is
implied.

What was used: the values of the int21 and int22 parameter tables, read from
the snapshot and transcribed into seqblaze's own parameter-ledger layout
(ledger units nndb2024-dna-int21 and nndb2024-dna-int22 under
params/ledger/values/, each value with its locator), from which the compiled
parameter pack is generated. No NNDB file is copied into or redistributed
with seqblaze. No licence or terms statement was found on the NNDB pages
consulted.

Resource citations (the NNDB asks to be cited by both):
  Mittal A, Turner DH, Mathews DH. NNDB: An expanded database of nearest
  neighbor parameters for predicting stability of nucleic acid secondary
  structures. J Mol Biol 2024;436(17):168549.
  doi:10.1016/j.jmb.2024.168549

  Turner DH, Mathews DH. NNDB: the nearest neighbor parameter database for
  predicting stability of nucleic acid secondary structure.
  Nucleic Acids Res 2010;38(Database issue):D280-D282.
  doi:10.1093/nar/gkp892

The NNDB credits its DNA parameter set to:
  Reuter JS, Mathews DH. RNAstructure: software for RNA secondary structure
  prediction and analysis. BMC Bioinformatics 2010;11:129.
  doi:10.1186/1471-2105-11-129

