Rust dependencies used for Result input hashing

These Rust crates are linked into seqblaze. Sequence-table identities
(merkle-blake3-v1) use blake3; index identities (merkle-sha256-v1) and the
other SHA-256 identities use sha2. Each crate is listed with the licence under
which seqblaze uses it, followed by the corresponding licence and copyright
notices. sha2 0.10.9 and the crates listed after it up to version_check are
each used under its MIT licence; arrayvec 0.7.8 and cpufeatures 0.3.1 are
used under their MIT licences; blake3 1.8.7 and constant_time_eq 0.4.2 are
used under the Apache License, Version 2.0, whose text is in LICENSE-APACHE,
in the same directory.

