CUDA backend (builds with the cuda feature)

seqblaze builds made with its cuda feature use the Rust crate cudarc 0.19.10
(https://crates.io/crates/cudarc/0.19.10; MIT OR Apache-2.0). cudarc loads the
NVIDIA CUDA driver library dynamically at run time; no NVIDIA library is
linked into or shipped with seqblaze. cudarc's pre-generated (bindgen) Rust
bindings to the CUDA driver API are compiled into such builds and are
distributed under cudarc's licence. The GPU code embedded in such builds (a
CUDA fatbin) is compiled by nvcc from seqblaze's own CUDA sources. Builds
without the cuda feature contain neither cudarc nor GPU code.
